==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
Stall as long as possible for Worker Cat levels. Be prepared for a big fight when you attack the enemy base. You will get knocked back and have to fight against a burrowing Zory and a Slow-inflicting Imperator Sael, both of which do some heavy area damage. Zory in particular will burrow and try to fight your backline while Sael will slow your front line and make it harder to keep him pushed forward.

Zory becomes the main priority to kill first (and each time he spawns), so a couple zombie killers are recommended. [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Lumbercat]] and [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Heavyweight Cat]] are great options here. Zigge is mainly an annoyance and free cash, but be careful of her Area Attack!

Proper planning and keeping up with reinforcements will secure you the win!

==='''Chapter 2'''===
This stage plays out basically the same as Chapter 1, but Sael has been switched out for a Cyberhorn. On one hand, Cyberhorn is slower and has barely any range, allowing him to be safely pelted at with ice from [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]]. But compared to the Sael in Chapter 1, he will shred your attackers MUCH more quickly if allowed to, with his high health making sure he sticks around for a while. Other than that, just treat it like it's Chapter 1 again.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
Chill Cat is once again useful since Cyberhorn is still present, but the much more pressing issue is Alpacky. Bring a sufficient Tanker to keep her stalled while your attackers chip away at her HP. The red enemies can be handled with [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]], and most anti-Zombie attackers will work against the rest of the enemies.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganglion]]: Has the same effective range as Alpacky, which means he requires a stepping stone. In addition to this, he is [[Strong Against]] both Aliens and Zombies, and he can Z-Kill any Zombie he hits.

